# Binary assets — never let Git apply line-ending conversion or text
# diffing to these, regardless of a contributor's local core.autocrlf
# setting. Without this, a Windows checkout with the common
# core.autocrlf=true default silently corrupts these files by rewriting
# LF byte sequences inside binary content (this is exactly what broke
# Campaign-01-Workbook.pdf for a contributor pulling on Windows).
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
